## Problem

`KafkaDataCachesDependencyInjection.AddKafkaCaches(...)` treated the two ways of configuring `KafkaCachesOptions` as mutually exclusive:

- a config **section name** bound from `IConfiguration`/appsettings, **or**
- a **delegate** (`Action<KafkaCachesOptions, IServiceProvider>`) that sets values in code.

When a user passed a delegate, the `else` branch ran and appsettings was **never bound** — the options object stood "just by itself", ignoring `IConfiguration`.

## Fix

Always bind the config section first (base/defaults), then layer the user delegate on top so code overrides/augments the bound config. This mirrors the bind-then-delegate pattern from our reference Kafka lib.

```csharp
var optionsBuilder = services.AddOptions<KafkaCachesOptions>(configsSectionName);
// Always bind the IConfiguration section first — it acts as the base / defaults.
optionsBuilder.Configure<IConfiguration>((opts, configuration) => {
    configuration.GetSection(configsSectionName).Bind(opts);
});
// Then layer the user delegate on top so code overrides/augments the bound config.
if (configsFactory is not null)
    services.AddTransient<IConfigureOptions<KafkaCachesOptions>>(sp => new ConfigureNamedOptions<KafkaCachesOptions>(
        configsSectionName, o => { configsFactory(o, sp); }));
```

`OptionsFactory<T>` applies registered `IConfigureOptions` in service-registration order, so the bind runs first and the delegate second: scalar values (e.g. `BootstrapServers`) set in code win, while `ClientSettings`/`Vars` dictionary entries merge.

## Scope

- Only the master overload changes; the four convenience overloads already funnel into it, so no public signatures change.
- Every existing call site already registers `IConfiguration`, so no caller breaks.
- Out of scope: `KafkaCachesGlobalOptions`, `KafkaCachesHealthOptions`, `DataCacheRegistryBuilder`.

## Tests

New wiring test `AddKafkaCaches_WithDelegate_BindsConfigurationThenAppliesDelegate` asserts the delegate overrides a bound `BootstrapServers` **and** a config-only `ClientSettings:foo` entry survives (proving the section is still bound). Full `Prague.Kafka.Tests` passes — 68/68 on net9.0 and net10.0.

